''s decathlon?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"8","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"12","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"7","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"10","is_correct":true}],"explanation":"Ten events over two days earn the decathlon winner the title of ''world''s greatest athlete''."},{"id":"q7","question":"Who holds the women''s 100 m world record of 10.49, set in 1988?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Florence Griffith-Joyner","is_correct":true},{"id":"b","text":"Marion Jones","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Shelly-Ann Fraser-Pryce","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Evelyn Ashford","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Florence Griffith-Joyner ran 10.49 in Indianapolis in 1988; the record has never been broken."},{"id":"q8","question":"How many Olympic gold medals did sprinter and long jumper Carl Lewis win?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"6","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"7","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"8","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"9","is_correct":true}],"explanation":"Carl Lewis collected nine Olympic golds between 1984 and 1996, including four straight long jump titles."}]'::jsonb,
